":"Low"},"numericFacets":{},"cardSignals":["Casual / Everyday Japanese Food","English B","Reservation: walk in"],"latestExternalRating":null,"coverImage":null,"demo":false},{"id":"8d798996-b657-56c1-935b-22b6a498fd54","slug":"satsuma-shuzo-meijigura","name":"Satsuma Shuzo Meijigura","localName":"薩摩酒造 花渡川蒸溜所 明治蔵","summary":"The site makes the role of koji, sweet potatoes, pot stills and ageing concrete inside one of Satsuma's historic production centres.","whyWorthwhile":"Its strongest decision-relevant feature is access to Handmade-style sweet-potato shochu production in a historic kura. The recommended visit is: Take the production/history route and taste contrasting shochu styles with a non-driving plan.","entityType":"food","countryCode":"JP","country":"Japan","region":"Kagoshima","locality":"Makurazaki","categories":["food-drink","sake-alcohol-production"],"subcategories":["sake-alcohol-production"],"tags":["imo shochu","earthenware pots","historic distilling"],"tier":"A","geometryType":"Point","centroid":[130.284929,31.271675],"bbox":[130.284929,31.271675,130.284929,31.271675],"customNamespace":"food","customFacets":{"food.primaryCategory":"Sake & Alcohol Production","food.japanRegion":"Kyushu","food.value":"exceptional","food.reservationClass":"walk-in","food.englishAccess":"B","food.localRecognition":"High","food.japaneseSpecialistRecognition":"High","food.internationalRecognition":"Low"},"numericFacets":{},"cardSignals":["Sake & Alcohol Production","English B","Reservation: walk in"],"latestExternalRating":null,"coverImage":null,"demo":false},{"id":"976bf98d-1a42-5200-b0ae-c158025c21f4","slug":"sushi-isono-kaori","name":"Sushi Isono Kaori","localName":"寿し いその香り","summary":"A focused sushi meal gives access to species and preparations tied to Yakushima's surrounding waters rather than generic resort seafood.","whyWorthwhile":"Its strongest decision-relevant feature is access to Yakushima local fish and flying-fish cuisine in sushi form. The recommended visit 